complexity_note: n is the length of `nums` and V the largest number.
why_time: Each different number has its bits counted in about log₂ V turns, and the 31 × 31 pairs of bit counts are a fixed amount of work.
why_space: The set of different numbers.
hint: In each place, a OR b and a AND b have two 1s between them when both a and b have a 1, one when only one of them does, and none otherwise. So the total is the 1 bits of a plus the 1 bits of b.
hint: Repeated numbers make the same pairs, so use `set(nums)`. Count how many different numbers have each number of 1 bits, from 0 to 30.
hint: Every two bit counts a and b with a + b ≥ k give `by_ones[a] * by_ones[b]` excellent pairs.
right: Turning each number into its count of 1 bits leaves only 31 kinds of number, so the pairs come from 31 × 31 multiplications instead of n² checks: O(n log V) in all.
